{"kind":{"type":"frontMatter","text":"title: \"Sync spins forever: a cancel flag nobody could set and a transport with no idle budget\"\u000adate: 2026-09-25\u000acategory: runtime-errors\u000amodule: rc-git-guard\u000aproblem_type: runtime_error\u000acomponent: infrastructure\u000asymptoms:\u000a  - \"The toolbar's sync button is replaced by a spinner that never stops; the button itself is hidden, so there is nothing to click\"\u000a  - \"Fetch, Pull, Push and Sync are all disabled in the Repository menu while the stuck transfer holds `isBusy`\"\u000a  - \"No error, no timeout; quitting the app is the only way out\"\u000a  - \"Reproduces with a dropped VPN, a sleeping laptop, or any peer that accepts the connection and then goes quiet\"\u000aroot_cause: api_misuse\u000aresolution_type: code_fix\u000aseverity: high\u000arelated_components:\u000a  - rc-git-ffi\u000a  - RcGitKit\u000a  - RcGitApp\u000atags: [gix, russh, tokio, cancellation, timeout, ffi, blocking-io, sync-io-bridge]"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":1},"runs":[{"text":"Sync spins forever: a cancel flag nobody could set and a transport with no idle budget","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Problem","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"rc-git-guard","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"'s remote operations already took a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"cancel: &AtomicBool","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and gix polls it while receiving a pack. Nothing could ever set it: the FFI built a fresh ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"AtomicBool::new(false)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" inside each call. Underneath that, the ssh transport's blocking reads had no time limit at all. A transfer that stopped moving had exactly two outcomes, success and forever.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Symptoms","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The toolbar spinner runs indefinitely. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"showSyncSpinner","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" set ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"syncButton?.isHidden = busy","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", so the one control that could have stopped it was off screen.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Every sync menu item validated against ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"!syncModel.isBusy","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and stayed disabled.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Nothing timed out: no error was ever presented, because no step ever returned.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Restarting the app was the only exit, which also threw away the evidence.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"What Didn't Work","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Reading the cancel parameter as if it were wired up.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"fetch_upstream","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"push_upstream","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" take a cancel flag and check it at every step boundary; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"receive()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" gets it as gix's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"should_interrupt","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". All of that was live code. The break was one layer up, at ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-ffi/src/lib.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", where each function created its own flag and dropped it on return. A parameter that exists is not a cancel path.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Expecting git config to supply the timeouts.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" gix reads ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"http.lowSpeedLimit","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"http.lowSpeedTime","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gitoxide.http.connectTimeout","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" into its curl options — but repositories here open with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"gix::open::Options::isolated()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", which reads no global or system config and no environment. Those keys can only come from code.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Passing ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"tokio::time::timeout(...)","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" to ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"block_on","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" The obvious spelling panics:","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"code","language":null,"text":"there is no reactor running, must be called from the context of a Tokio 1.x runtime"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The arguments are evaluated first, so the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Sleep","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is constructed before ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"block_on","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" enters the runtime context. The pre-existing ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"SshWrite::drop","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" had the same latent shape.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Solution","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"One flag that outlives the call.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Cancel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" wraps ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Arc<AtomicBool>","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and replaces the bare borrow on ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"fetch_upstream","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"push_upstream","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and the pack helpers ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"count_pack","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"write_pack","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (the CLI's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"sync","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" verb runs fetch, pull and push in turn), so the ssh transport can hold a share of it after the function that built the transport has returned (","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/remote.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":").","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Poll instead of block.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Watch::drive","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"crates/rc-git-guard/src/actions/remote/ssh/session.rs","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" replaces ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"SyncIoBridge","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"'s plain blocking read. Each channel read and write is polled in short slices:","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"code","language":"rust","text":"let started = Instant::now();\u000alet mut operation = pin!(operation);\u000aloop {\u000a    if self.cancel.load(Ordering::SeqCst) {\u000a        return Err(io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::Interrupted, ...));\u000a    }\u000a    // The timer is built inside the async block on purpose: constructing a\u000a    // `Sleep` needs the runtime context, which `block_on` only enters once it\u000a    // has the future in hand.\u000a    let waited = handle\u000a        .block_on(async { tokio::time::timeout(CANCEL_POLL, operation.as_mut()).await });\u000a    match waited {\u000a        Ok(result) => return result,\u000a        Err(_elapsed) if started.elapsed() >= self.idle => return Err(timed_out),\u000a        Err(_elapsed) => {}\u000a    }\u000a}"},"runs":[],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The future is pinned once and re-polled; an elapsed slice drops only the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Timeout","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" wrapper, so nothing the peer already sent is lost. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"CANCEL_POLL","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is 200 ms, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"IDLE_TIMEOUT","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" 120 s, and the clock restarts on every call, so it measures the gap between bytes rather than the length of the transfer.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Timeouts in code for curl.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"http_timeouts","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" sets ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"connect_timeout","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" to 30 s and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"low_speed_limit_bytes_per_second: 1","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"low_speed_time_seconds: 120","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" — \"fail when fewer than one byte moves for two minutes\", which never punishes a slow link. Fetch applies it with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"connection.set_transport_options(...)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", seeded from ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"repo.transport_options()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" so a repository's own ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"http.proxy","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" survives; push, which builds its transport by hand, applies it with ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"transport.configure(&options)","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" because ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"connect::Options","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" carries no HTTP settings.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A handle across the ABI.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"RcGitCancel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (opaque, ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"rcgit_cancel_new","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" / ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"_signal","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" / ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"_free","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":") is the one FFI handle meant to be touched from a second thread — the thread inside a transfer cannot ask itself to stop. ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"RCGIT_CANCELLED","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" (-5) keeps a cancel from being reported as a failure. Swift's ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"CancelToken","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" frees it in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"deinit","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", and ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"SyncModel","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" mints one per workflow so a signalled token is never reused.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A control that stays on screen.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" While busy the toolbar button becomes ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"stop.circle","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" wired to ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"cancelSync","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":", with the spinner beside it rather than in place of it, plus Repository ▸ Cancel Sync on ⌘.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Why This Works","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A cancel has to reach the thread that is blocked, and that thread cannot check anything while it sits in a blocking ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"read","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":". Slicing the wait is what turns an un-interruptible call into an interruptible one; the ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Arc","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is what lets the flag reach it. The idle budget covers the case the user is not watching — a dead TCP connection produces no bytes and no error, so only a clock can end it. 120 s is safe because a git server sends keepalives every few seconds while it thinks, so that much total silence means the connection is gone, not that the repository is large.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"The costs are nil on the happy path: one relaxed atomic load per I/O chunk (gix already does this while receiving a pack), and a timer only while the socket is silent.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"heading","level":2},"runs":[{"text":"Prevention","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":0,"marker":null},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Nothing may have only \"success\" and \"forever\" as outcomes.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" The same rule the updater learned at the process level applies at the socket level. Every blocking call in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"actions/remote/","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" gets a cancel poll and an idle budget; ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".claude/rules/guard.md","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" now says so.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"A cancel parameter is not a cancel path.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Trace it to something a second thread can set. A flag constructed inside the callee is dead code that reads as a feature.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"An isolated open means configuration comes from code.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Options::isolated()","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" is a safety property here, and the cost is that any gix behavior normally tuned through git config — timeouts included — has to be set explicitly.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Build a tokio timer inside the ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"async","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" block, never as an argument to ","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"block_on","style":["strong","code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":".","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" A ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Sleep","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" needs the runtime context that ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"block_on","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" has not entered yet.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
{"kind":{"type":"paragraph"},"runs":[{"text":"Verify a cancellation test by breaking it.","style":["strong"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" Disabling the flag check in ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Watch::drive","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" makes ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"a_cancel_raised_while_blocked_wakes_the_operation","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" hang to the harness cap and fail; a cancellation test that still passes with the check removed is not testing anything. The idle budget is a ","style":[],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":"Watch","style":["code"],"link":null,"image":false},{"text":" field rather than the constant so the same test can measure it in milliseconds.","style":[],"link":null,"image":false}],"quoteDepth":0,"listDepth":1,"marker":"bullet"},
